

🎓 Day 39: Student Database Using File Storage


📌 Project Overview


This is my Day 39 Python project, where I built a Student Database that stores student records in a text file called students.txt.

The program allows users to add students, view all student records, search by roll number, calculate the class average, find the topper, delete student records, and update marks.

Each student record is stored in this format:

roll,name,marks

Example:

101,Arun,85.0
102,Priya,92.0
103,Kumar,78.0

Unlike programs that store information only in variables, this project uses file storage to keep student records available after the program closes.

It also introduces functions for loading and saving records, lists of tuples, searching, and calculating results.


